 "title": "Low-voltage SPDT analog switch, 2:1 multiplexer / demultiplexer bus switch",
 "source": {
  "revision": "NC7SB3157/D Rev. 4, June 2024",
  "pages": 11
 },
 "summary": "A single-pole double-throw CMOS switch: one common port A connects to B0 or B1 according to the select input S, with break-before-make changeover. It runs from 1.65 V to 5.5 V, passes signals from rail to rail, and has 3.0 Ω typical on resistance at VCC = 4.5 V. The control input is rated to 7.0 V and is high-impedance when powered down. Sold in a 6-lead SC70 and a 6-lead MicroPak.",
 "key_figures": [
  [
   "Supply",
   "1.65 V to 5.5 V"
  ],
  [
   "On resistance",
   "3.0 Ω typ, 7.0 Ω max at VCC = 4.5 V, IO = 30 mA"
  ],
