   },
   "note": "",
   "page": 4
  }
 ],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Switch action",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "S low connects B0 to A; S high connects B1 to A. On a change of S the closed side opens before the other closes, so the two B ports are never briefly joined through A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Signal path",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The switch is a CMOS pass element, usable in analog and in digital applications. Signals may swing from 0 to VCC. As a bus switch it adds no propagation delay other than the RC of its on resistance and the load."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Control input",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "S has an absolute maximum of +7.0 V, and the control input is over-voltage tolerant to 7.0 V; the device description gives 5.5 V as the control voltage it tolerates independent of VCC. S is high-impedance with the part powered down. It has to be held high or low at all times. Logic thresholds scale with VCC: 0.7 VCC high and 0.3 VCC low from 2.3 V to 5.5 V, 0.75 VCC and 0.25 VCC from 1.65 V to 1.95 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "On resistance",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "RON is 3.0 Ω typ (7.0 Ω max) at VCC = 4.5 V with the input at 0 V, and 17.0 Ω typ (50.0 Ω max) at VCC = 1.65 V with the input at 1.65 V. Typical on resistance is under 10 Ω at VCC = 3.3 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pin one",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Reading the top mark left to right, pin one is the lower left pin. The SC70 and MicroPak share one pin order."
  }
 ],
